# Options and errors

[Back to Monte Carlo](../finance_04_monte_carlo.md)

## Every option

| `field.controls.mc` | Meaning | Default | Requirement |
|---|---|---|---|
| `paths` | the number of simulated paths | 40000 | positive |
| `steps` | the number of time steps per path | 252 | positive |
| `scheme` | the variance scheme ([Simulated paths](simulated_paths.md)) | `Euler` | |
| `rand_method` | `Pseudo`, `Sobol`, `Halton`, `Torus` ([Quasi-random sequences](quasi_random_sequences.md)) | `Pseudo` | |
| `randomized_quasi` | randomise the quasi-random sequence | false | |
| `sobol_scrambling` | the Sobol scrambling variant | 0 | 0 to 3 |
| `antithetic` | antithetic pairs ([Variance reduction](variance_reduction.md)) | false | |
| `control_variate` | the Black-Scholes control | false | |
| `control_vol` | the control's volatility; 0 means the long-run volatility of the model | 0 | finite and non-negative |
| `importance_sampling` | shift the asset shocks and reweight | false | |
| `importance_shift` | the per-step shift of the asset shocks | 0 | finite |
| `seed` | the random stream | 0 | |
| `offset` | where a quasi-random sequence starts | 0 | |
| `basis_degree` | American and Bermudan options only: the degree of the continuation-value regression ([The pricing field](../finance_06_the_pricing_field.md)) | 3 | positive |

The estimate of one run is a single number; the number of paths and steps should be chosen against the error bar found by repeating with different seeds ([Pricing by simulation](pricing_by_simulation.md)). One path is allowed and returns that path's discounted payoff.

## Conditions and messages

A field checks its Monte Carlo controls when it prices, and reports each violation by name.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>
#include <limits>

namespace fin = pluss::subsp::math::finance;
namespace mod = fin::module;
namespace prc = fin::pricing;
using namespace pluss::tils;
using pluss::Series;

constexpr double kSpot = 100.0, kRate = 0.03, kDiv = 0.01;
const std::vector<double> kHeston{1.5, 0.04, 0.3, -0.7, 0.04};

// A call under the given model, priced (or simulated) by Monte Carlo; the controls in field.controls.mc are the caller's to set.
mod::Field monte_carlo(fin::model::Kind kind, const std::vector<double> &params, double strike = 100.0, double maturity = 1.0) {
  return mod::Field{.instrument = fin::instrument::make(prc::Call, strike, maturity),
                    .market = fin::market::make(kSpot, kRate, kDiv),
                    .model = fin::model::make(kind, params),
                    .controls = {.engine = mod::Engine::MonteCarlo, .risk = mod::Risk::PriceOnly}};
}
// The COS price of the same Heston call: the reference the simulation is judged against.
double cos_reference(double strike, const std::vector<double> &params = kHeston, double maturity = 1.0) {
  mod::Field f = monte_carlo(fin::model::Kind::Heston, params, strike, maturity);
  f.controls.engine = mod::Engine::Cos;
  return f.price().price.items<double>()[0];
}
double price1(const mod::Field &f) { return f.price().price.items<double>()[0]; }
// Mean and standard deviation of a set of repeated prices.
std::pair<double, double> mean_sd(const std::vector<double> &x) {
  double mean = 0.0;
  for (double v : x) mean += v / x.size();
  double variance = 0.0;
  for (double v : x) variance += (v - mean) * (v - mean) / (x.size() - 1);
  return {mean, std::sqrt(variance)};
}

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  auto attempt = [&](const char *label, auto edit) {
    mod::Field field = monte_carlo(fin::model::Kind::Heston, kHeston);
    field.controls.mc.paths = 2000;
    field.controls.mc.steps = 16;
    edit(field.controls.mc);
    try {
      out.writeln(label, "-> price", price1(field));
    } catch (const std::exception &e) {
      const std::string message = e.what();
      out.writeln(label, "->", message.substr(0, message.find('\n')));
    }
  };
  attempt("paths = 0              ", [](auto &mc) { mc.paths = 0; });
  attempt("steps = 0              ", [](auto &mc) { mc.steps = 0; });
  attempt("paths = 1              ", [](auto &mc) { mc.paths = 1; });
  attempt("importance_shift = NaN ", [](auto &mc) { mc.importance_sampling = true; mc.importance_shift = std::numeric_limits<double>::quiet_NaN(); });
  attempt("control_vol = -1       ", [](auto &mc) { mc.control_variate = true; mc.control_vol = -1.0; });
  attempt("sobol_scrambling = 7   ", [](auto &mc) { mc.rand_method = fin::volatility::RandMethod::Sobol; mc.randomized_quasi = true; mc.sobol_scrambling = 7; });
  {{
    mod::Field field = monte_carlo(fin::model::Kind::Heston, kHeston, 90.0, 0.0);
    out.writeln("maturity 0 (intrinsic value, call struck at 90) ->", price1(field));
  }}
}
```

Each invalid setting is rejected with a message that names the control. One path is a valid run, and it prices the option at that path's discounted payoff (0 here, as the single path ends below the strike). A zero maturity returns the intrinsic value.

